THOUGHT: NullAway complains because the parameter v is annotated @Nullable but is dereferenced without a null check. I should preserve the API (keep @Nullable) and add a defensive null check. A reasonable behavior is to no-op (return this) when v is null, which avoids introducing new semantics elsewhere. After changing the method, I’ll run the NullAway-checked compilation to ensure the error count drops by one and no new errors appear.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/libgdx && sed -i '88,92c\  @Override
  public Vector2 set(@Nullable Vector2 v) {
    if (v == null) return this;
    x = v.x;
    y = v.y;
    return this;
  }' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/math/Vector2.java && ./gradlew gdx:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -E "NullAway|errors" new_build_output.log | tail -n 5
```

